interesting_fun_fact = ["Wind Turbines are used to produce pollution free electricity","Hubble space telescope provides information about stars","Andromeda is of the billions of galaxy known to humans ", "🪶 Galileo’s Falling Bodies: Galileo found that, neglecting air drag, a feather (in vacuum) and a hammer fall at the same acceleration (~10 m/s² near Earth). That’s a cornerstone of classical mechanics.",
    "👁️‍🗨️ Meniscus Reading: When reading liquid level in a measuring cylinder, you must keep your eye at the same level as the lowest point of the meniscus. Otherwise you over- or under-estimate the volume—an everyday trick for accurate lab work.",
    "🚂 Relative Motion: A passenger sitting in a moving train is “at rest” relative to the train interior but “in motion” relative to an observer on the platform. There is no absolute rest frame; motion only has meaning relative to something else.",
    "💥 Momentum Matters: A bullet has small mass but high speed, giving it significant momentum; conversely, a slow-moving truck can have enormous impact due to its large mass, illustrating why momentum = mass × velocity matters.",
    "🛞 No Friction, No Grip: Imagine friction vanishing: cars couldn’t start or stop, you couldn’t walk (no grip), objects slide endlessly, braking is impossible.",
    "🧊 Iceberg Buoyancy: Ice has about 9 percent lower density than liquid water, so roughly 9/10 of an iceberg’s volume is below the surface. This is a dramatic illustration of Archimedes’ principle and density differences.",
    "🚗 Hydraulic Brakes (Pascal’s Law): Pascal’s law (pressure transmitted undiminished in a fluid) makes hydraulic brakes possible: a small force on the brake lever becomes a larger force at the brake pads.",
    "🏔️ Boiling Point at Altitude: At higher altitudes, atmospheric pressure is lower, so boiling point of water is lower. Thus water boils “sooner” but at lower temperature—cooking times change.",
    "🌡️ Thermal Expansion in Structures: Large steel or concrete structures expand/contract with temperature; bearings or sliding joints let parts move slightly, preventing damage.",
    "💧 Evaporative Cooling (Sweat): When sweat (liquid) evaporates from your skin, it takes latent heat from your body, lowering your skin’s temperature.",
    "🐙 Deep-Sea Pressure Adaptations: To survive high pressures, some deep-sea organisms have flexible or gelatinous bodies so they’re not crushed by immense water pressure."]

